OL,3,GNEWSAAverage NI house price now above
OL,4,A#200,000
OL,5,
OL,6,FThe average price of a house in
OL,7,FNorthern Ireland has risen above
OL,8,F#200,000 for the first time since the
OL,9,Fproperty crash of the late 2000s,
OL,10,Faccording to official figures.
OL,12,FIn the second quarter of this year the
OL,13,Faverage price was just under #202,500.
OL,15,FThat is almost exactly the same price
OL,16,Flevel reached in the final quarter of
OL,17,F2007, just as a property bubble was
OL,18,Fbeginning to burst.
OL,20,FHowever, the effects of inflation mean
OL,21,Fthat houses are still substantially
OL,22,Fcheaper in real terms today.
OL,23,APub: 19-AugQppppppppppppppppppppppppppp
